 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Assigned {{v3}}/bench-repo issue #4 \"{{v1}}\" to bench-assignee via the issue sidebar Assignees picker (opened it, selected bench-assignee, then closed the picker). Verified: the sidebar now displays \"bench-assignee (Bench Assignee)\" as the sole assignee (the \"No Assignees\" empty placeholder is hidden, admin is NOT assigned), the combo's hidden assignee_ids value is \"3\", and the update request /{{v3}}/bench-repo/issues/assignee?issue_ids=4 actually fired. The assignment persisted across a full page reload, and the issue's existing bug + priority-high labels remain. Key mechanism found earlier attempts missed: these multi-select sidebar combos only send their AJAX update when the dropdown is hidden (onHide → doUpdate), so selecting an option is not enough — the picker must be closed. (assignee_applied: Bench Assignee)",
